#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Generate/check the Step 1 data-model declaration inventory.

The only repository inputs are read by `git show` at the pins below; the
external manifest and the hand-curated DRAFT classification are validated
before an inventory is written. --check compares the complete generated bytes.
Exit status: 0 success, 1 invalid content/stale fixture, 2 I/O or usage.

This is deliberately a declaration parser, not a C preprocessor or compiler.
It supports simple typedefs, structs, enums, nonnegative int-safe integer
expressions and declarators. Reached declarations reject literals and embedded
directives; referenced integer macros must be single tokens or fully parenthesized
expressions unless the macro name is the entire array bound. Referenced macros
may not be undefined or have differing definitions in any read source. Unknown
constructs, duplicate names, unknown types, ambiguous constants, unresolved
expressions and nonterminal zero-length arrays are rejected. It does not infer
a C ABI or evaluate preprocessor conditionals: the manifest records the selected
LP64 platform mappings and cited definitions are compared after normalizing
comments/whitespace. Conditional definitions, casts, function pointers,
anonymous aggregates, signed/overflowing expressions and macro-generated fields
in a reachable declaration require a reviewed parser/baseline change. Changing
a pin requires an independent re-extraction and review of the manifest, source
conditional context and the draft classification; --check is not such a review.
"""
